swehouse.c: SEFLG_RADIANS left the speeds in degrees

The positions are converted and the two speed arrays are not, so a caller asking
for radians is handed the two in different units, a factor of 57.3 apart.

    swe_houses_ex2(2451545.0, SEFLG_RADIANS, 52.5, 13.4, 'P', ...)
      cusp[1]        0.900328369   radians
      cusp_speed[1]  600.727650279 degrees per day, beside it
      after          10.484675405  radians per day

Conformance rather than a change of contract: swephprg documents the parameters
as cusp_speed /* like cusps */ and ascmc_speed /* like ascmc */, and under that
flag they were not like them. It does change what the flag returns, so a caller
who had compensated for the old behaviour will have to stop.

Part of an eight-step series. Applied in order, the eight produce a file
byte-identical to the single patch "swehouse.c: compute house cusp speeds
analytically"; take either the series or that patch, not both. Every step
compiles. Steps 01 to 06 also apply to a clean tree on their own, so any one of
them can be taken without the rest; 07 needs 01 to 05, not 06; 08 needs all seven to link. Do not
drop 02 or 04 from the middle: nothing else needs them, so the result still
builds clean and is quietly wrong.

---
 swehouse.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
diff --git a/swehouse.c b/swehouse.c
index 892c931..5172eab 100644
--- a/swehouse.c
+++ b/swehouse.c
@@ -397,6 +397,19 @@ int CALL_CONV swe_houses_ex2(double tjd_ut,
       cusp[i] *= DEGTORAD;
     for (i = 0; i < SE_NASCMC; i++)
       ascmc[i] *= DEGTORAD;
+    /* The speeds are angles per day and belong in the same unit as the angles
+     * they accompany. Without this a SEFLG_RADIANS caller was handed radian
+     * positions beside degree per day speeds, so anything that added a speed
+     * to a position, or compared the two, was out by a factor of 57.3. The
+     * omission predates this patch and mattered less while nine house systems
+     * returned interpolated speeds nobody could rely on; now that every system
+     * returns a real derivative, callers will use it. */
+    if (cusp_speed != NULL)
+      for (i = 1; i <= ito; i++)
+        cusp_speed[i] *= DEGTORAD;
+    if (ascmc_speed != NULL)
+      for (i = 0; i < SE_NASCMC; i++)
+        ascmc_speed[i] *= DEGTORAD;
   }
   if (retc_makr < 0)
     return retc_makr;
